From 9d74ecb0f8786c7c5f57ed2cdac286c9bc750b3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:45:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: memory cards via HLE MCSERV, generic IOP->EE RPC
 service, NTSC vblank, smaller fixes

- Memory cards: SIO2 is not emulated, so MCMAN/MCSERV requested by modload
  always load through the HLE provider (host-file cards); it reports the
  MCSERV 2.1 / MCMAN 2.3 versions the GA2 discs ship (libmc rejected older
  ones). Both games now detect a formatted card.
- Generic reverse RPC: without game-specific hooks, an IOP call to an EE RPC
  server runs the registered sceSifServeData func(fno, buff, size) as a
  guest invocation and returns the 64 reply bytes (Mugen needs this).
- VBlank pacing and cycle period are NTSC 60000/1001 Hz.
- GIF arbiter reuses packet buffers and skips sorting single packets; pgs
  readback copies raw pixels on the game thread and converts on the present
  thread.
- Diagnostics: GA2_WATCHDOG=<s> samples the EE pc; GA2_SYSCALL_TRACE logs
  SetSyscall/FindAddress.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
